    <briefdescription>
<para>Optional context attached to an incident for diagnostics. </para>
    </briefdescription>
    <detaileddescription>
<para><simplesect kind="warning"><para><bold>Lifetime contract</bold>: All <computeroutput>std::string_view</computeroutput> fields are non-owning. Callers MUST ensure the underlying string storage outlives the incident and any handler invocation that may persist it (e.g., into a log buffer or metrics system). Passing a temporary <computeroutput>std::string</computeroutput> or a local char array whose lifetime ends before the handler returns will result in undefined behaviour. If the incident may outlive the emitting stack frame, store the strings in a stable buffer (e.g., a <computeroutput>static constexpr</computeroutput> literal or a heap-allocated string) and construct <computeroutput><ref refid="structthemis_1_1timeseries_1_1_incident_context" kindref="compound">IncidentContext</ref></computeroutput> from that stable storage. </para>
</simplesect>
</para>
